{
  "version": 2,
  "notes": "Synthetic, deterministic datasets with injected changes. expect.rules are the anomaly rules the change is designed to trigger; entities are SKUs a good report names; forbidden are claims a report must never make. Deterministic answer keys (checked for every policy): verdicts are the server's judgements of its candidate hypotheses, dominance the larger effect of each decomposition (mix/rate, price/basket), streaks the history direction and minimum run length, low_sample SKUs that must be flagged, recheck the states of this case's hypotheses re-judged on a follow-up period, intent the routing of a question. Model answer keys: causes is a list of injected causes, each a list of alternative matchers ({sku}, {hypothesis}, {tool, metric} against supported hypotheses cited by findings, or {ruled_out} against the ruled-out list); distractors must not be cited ({sku} as above, {note} a substring of a cited merchant note). followups (case level) are earlier action items whose recommendation is re-evaluated on this period by the report service's rule (previous period as the source report, optional skus for its scope); expect.followups are the states that check_recommendation must report, in order. live_only cases need a model's judgement and are skipped by the offline suite; expect.kind is the reply kind a question must get (answer, clarify, suggested_query).",
